# 📅 MCP Monday Server

A **production-grade MCP server** for Monday.com integration, built with
[`chuk-mcp-runtime`](https://pypi.org/project/chuk-mcp-runtime/) and following
[IBM Consulting Advantage MCP standards](https://github.ibm.com/advantage-mcp/mcp-standards).

## 🔎 Overview

The **MCP Monday Server** provides a complete set of tools to interact with **Monday.com workspaces**,
enabling developers and agents to:

- **Boards**: list, create, and manage boards, groups, and columns
- **Items**: create, update, move, delete, archive, and fetch items and subitems
- **Updates**: post and retrieve updates with attached files
- **Files**: retrieve files from items and updates
- **Docs**: list, create, and manage documents and content blocks

All tools use structured JSON logging with sensitive-data redaction, Pydantic I/O validation,
correlation-ID tracing, and automatic retry with exponential backoff.

---

## ✨ Features

- 22 MCP tools covering all core Monday.com operations
- SSE transport on port 8080 (configurable via `config.yaml`)
- `httpx`-based async HTTP client with connection pooling and retry logic
- Structured JSON logging (redacts API keys and tokens automatically)
- Pydantic v2 input/output schemas with validation
- Production-ready UBI9 container (3-stage build, non-root user, healthcheck)
- Full devops stack: `Makefile`, `Containerfile`, `make podman`, `make trivy`

---

## ⚙️ Quick Start

```bash
git clone https://github.ibm.com/advantage-mcp/monday.git
cd monday

# Set up the virtual environment and install dependencies
make install

# Copy and configure environment variables
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env — set MCP_MONDAY_API_KEY at minimum

# Run the server (SSE on port 8080 by default)
make serve
```

The server starts at `http://0.0.0.0:8080/sse`.

---

## 🔐 Environment Variables

| Variable | Required | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `MCP_MONDAY_API_KEY` | ✅ Yes | — | Monday.com Personal API token |
| `MCP_MONDAY_WORKSPACE_URL` | No | — | Base URL for building item/doc links (e.g. `https://acme.monday.com`) |
| `MCP_MONDAY_TIMEOUT` | No | `30` | Request timeout in seconds |
| `MCP_MONDAY_MAX_RETRIES` | No | `3` | Max retry attempts on timeout/network error |
| `MCP_MONDAY_LOG_LEVEL` | No | `INFO` | Log level: `DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, `ERROR` |
| `MCP_MONDAY_LOG_FORMAT` | No | `json` | Log format: `json` (production) or `text` (development) |
| `MCP_MONDAY_ENVIRONMENT` | No | `production` | Environment identifier |

---

## 🛠 Available Tools

### 📋 Boards

| Tool | Description |
|---|---|
| `list_boards` | List all boards (paginated) |
| `get_board_groups` | Get all groups in a board |
| `get_board_columns` | Get all columns of a board (with label values) |
| `create_board` | Create a new board |
| `create_board_group` | Create a new group inside a board |

### 📌 Items

| Tool | Description |
|---|---|
| `list_items_in_groups` | List items in groups with cursor pagination |
| `list_subitems_in_items` | List subitems for a set of parent items |
| `create_item` | Create a top-level item or subitem |
| `update_item` | Update column values on an item |
| `create_update` | Post a text update on an item |
| `get_item_by_id` | Fetch full item data by ID |
| `get_item_updates` | Get updates (comments) for an item |
| `move_item_to_group` | Move an item to a different group |
| `delete_item` | Delete an item |
| `archive_item` | Archive an item |

### 📎 Files

| Tool | Description |
|---|---|
| `get_item_files` | Get files attached to an item |
| `get_update_files` | Get files attached to an update |

### 📑 Docs

| Tool | Description |
|---|---|
| `get_docs` | List documents |
| `get_doc_content` | Get content blocks of a document |
| `create_doc` | Create a document in a workspace or board |
| `add_doc_block` | Add a content block to a document |

---

## 📂 Project Structure

```
mcp-monday-server/
├── Containerfile              # 3-stage UBI9 production container
├── Makefile                   # All devops targets (make help for full list)
├── config.yaml                # SSE transport config (port 8080)
├── pyproject.toml             # Project + tool configuration (PEP 621)
├── .env.example               # Environment variable template
├── CONTRIBUTING.md            # Contribution guidelines
└── src/
    └── mcp_monday_server/
        ├── main.py            # Entrypoint — loads config, starts runtime
        ├── config.py          # Pydantic configuration model
        ├── logging_config.py  # JSON structured logging with redaction
        ├── exceptions.py      # Typed exception hierarchy
        ├── clients/
        │   ├── base_client.py    # Async httpx client with retry/backoff
        │   └── monday_client.py  # Monday.com GraphQL client singleton
        └── tools/
            ├── schemas.py        # Pydantic Input/Output schemas
            ├── list_boards.py
            ├── get_board_groups.py
            └── ...               # One file per tool
```

---

## 🐳 Container

```bash
# Build
make podman

# Run (reads MCP_MONDAY_API_KEY from environment)
make podman-run

# Stop
make podman-stop

# Security scan
make trivy
```

